implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL WHOLE-EPIC REVIEW, HANDOFF, CLEANUP (I06 rev-2 step 4; DoD 5). Load adversarial-self-review.

Read the whole CQ-I diff at $SHA: `git show` each commit in step 1's list. That list includes I06d and 5e816f2c, which the description omits but which are CQ-I. Hunt for what the slices got wrong about each other. Each item ends as one of: verified (cite file:line), fixed forward (TRIAGE 3), or a filed or owned row.
- Producer and consumer:
  - vm-control's schemas (moe-vm-status-v1, -reconcile-v1, -cleanup-v1) and codes against ManagedVmPresentation.kt and moe-vscode/src/util/ManagedVm.ts. A code with no bundle text renders as unknown in both; the wording difference noted in I05 is consistent or has an owner.
  - Approvals: every IDE approval route sends the rendered expectedPlanRevision. F04b's revision-less refusal and PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH reach the user as actionable text in both IDEs.
  - CLIENT_HELLO: the daemon supports it and no IDE sends it, by decision.
- Activation: grep both clients. No UPDATE_SETTINGS path sends executionProfile or deliveryPolicy, neither IDE offers verified-local, and strongProfile is always blocked.
- Reconnect: a disconnect with a pending approval is never confirmed (corpus rows; I06a). The daemon resets per-socket negotiation on reconnect (I01 tests).
- Windows:
  - vm-control receives paths with spaces and drive letters as argument arrays with no shell (JetBrains ProcessBuilder list, VS Code execFile array).
  - CQ-I03a's hand-forward (comment-ef257bf0 on task-4e412148): ownedLedgerDir resolves the same directory for D:/x, D:\x and /mnt/d/x; cleanup deletes only ledger-owned VMs with a non-open owner attempt and a free lease; below Node 22 it preserves everything; the list_resources-to-delete race is a documented residual.
- Packaging: steps 1-2 show no test artifacts, and every required helper is present.
- Docs: CQ-I06e's DEVELOPMENT.md, README and plugin.xml text matches the landed code and this evidence, and claims no per-platform result.
- Rails: no .moe edits and no Git writes in the epic diff; none of globalRails.forbiddenPatterns in its added lines; verified-local untouched.

Residuals: give each one an owner task id, or 'unowned: human decision' after moe.search_tasks. File a row only for a real, unowned defect. Known so far:
- the profile/evidence status UI (I02 note; V06);
- JetBrains re-arming after PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH: check whether I06d 12fd4333 resolved it;
- VS Code JSON.parse accepting lossy literals;
- cleanup preserving everything below Node 22 and at bindHost 0.0.0.0;
- the npm moe-proxy package shipping compiled tests;
- SettingsPanel saying 'Settings saved.' after a failed send (I04);
- producer codes with no bundle text;
- ManagedVmPanel's stdout capture, unbounded until timeout (I03);
- the VS Code vm-control child inheriting the extension-host env (I05);
- headless only: no runIde or Extension Host run.

If this task fixed anything forward: copy the edited files into $SNAP and $WIN, cmp them, re-run the owning suite, and re-run B1 fresh under the lease. That run is complete_task's evidence.

Close-out:
- Write the Serena memory 'task-task-426a012ecc374cdaa7454742bc5a552a-handoff'. Include:
  - $SHA;
  - one line per run (A1-A8, B1-B2, W1-W6) with counts and engine/version;
  - the residual owners;
  - 'pending CQ-R13';
  - I06's re-run trigger: if `git diff $SHA..HEAD -- scripts/local-runner moe-jetbrains moe-vscode` is non-empty, re-run A5, A6 and B1.
- Post that pointer as one moe.add_comment on task-4e412148225f480c8c0d5a1706a3cc76.
- Delete $SNAP and $WIN by their recorded paths. Kill only PIDs this session started.
- complete_task with B1's command (labelled as the Windows equivalent), its exit code and its output tail, plus one line per run.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
Gate and review the CQ-I client epic ahead of R13's certification reports, at one recorded SHA that includes CQ-I06e.
- A Linux snapshot runs one fresh full regression: daemon, proxy, claude-plugin, VS Code, the CI local-runner line, a VS Code bundle built from fresh dists with its packaged onboarding checks, and lint.
- A Windows copy of the same SHA covers:
  - the gradle gate: gradlew.bat test --rerun under the jetbrains-gradle lease, labelled as the Windows equivalent;
  - a real JetBrains zip with its packaged onboarding checks;
  - the CI windows-latest wrapper suites under Windows node, each labelled with its engine (PowerShell 5.1 or pwsh 7);
  - `cli.mjs prerequisites` on both Nodes.
- Native host certification is recorded only as 'pending CQ-R13'.
- One adversarial review of the whole CQ-I diff ends with every finding fixed forward in its owning module, or filed as an owned row.
No runtime behaviour changes beyond a bounded fix-forward.

